    <p>Both dynasties employed a feudal system of land grants (known as <em>veedhi</em> or <em>agraharam</em>) to Brahmins and military officials, ensuring loyalty and facilitating revenue collection. Their armies were organized into infantry, cavalry, and a formidable war‑elephant corps, enabling rapid territorial expansion across the Deccan plateau.</p>

