    <li><strong>Tulsidas (Uttar Pradesh, 16th c.)</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Authored the <em>Ramcharitmanas</em> in Awadhi, making the story of Rama accessible to the masses.</li>
            <li>Promoted the concept of “Rama as the universal lord” and reinforced moral virtues.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Chaitanya Mahaprabhu (Bengal, 15th c.)</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Propagated the worship of Krishna in the form of Radha‑Krishna.</li>
